    history: "Chandi Padvo, celebrated on the full moon night of the Sharad season (Sharad Purnima), is one of Surat's most beloved and uniquely celebrated festivals. According to Hindu tradition, the moon on this particular full moon night emits special healing rays that infuse 'amrit' (divine nectar) into foods left under the open sky. Families across Surat prepare dishes of sweetened flattened rice (doodh-poha) soaked in chilled milk and left under the moonlight to receive the moon's blessings overnight. The celebration involves community gatherings in building compounds, cultural programmes, folk music, and traditional games. It is a deeply intimate festival that reflects Surat's close-knit residential community culture — neighbours who barely interact during busy weekdays unite joyfully on this night.",
    address: "Residential Societies & Open Grounds across Surat",
    time: "October (Sharad Purnima — Full Moon Night)",
    tip: "Join a local society's Chandi Padvo celebration to experience authentic community bonding — most societies welcome outsiders warmly. Enjoy doodh-poha and chikki under the moonlight. The atmosphere is peaceful, musical, and deeply community-oriented.",
