    history: "Ponk is perhaps Surat's most unique and season-specific food — a dish that is almost completely unknown outside of South Gujarat and celebrated with passionate, near-religious fervour within the city during winter months. Ponk refers to tender, freshly harvested green sorghum (jowar) grains that are lightly roasted or steamed and eaten with a variety of accompaniments. In Surat, seasonal ponk vendors set up special stalls from November to February, serving it with ghee, jaggery, fresh lime, sev, and chilli powder. More adventurously, ponk is used as an ingredient in ponk vada (deep-fried crispy fritters), ponk khichdi, and ponk pattice. The entire city seems to participate in eating ponk during the season — it is a shared culinary moment that uniquely defines the Surati winter experience.",
