    history: "A traditional Surati wedding is a multi-day, multi-event celebration that is legendary even within Gujarat for its lavishness, warmth, and extraordinary food. Surati weddings typically involve ceremonies spanning 3–5 days, beginning with the mehendi and haldi functions, followed by the garba-sangeet night, the main wedding ceremony, and concluding with a grand reception. What makes Surati weddings truly exceptional is the food — wedding feasts in Surat are served in large community halls (vadi) where hundreds of guests are seated in long rows and served a succession of dishes that can run to 50+ items. Local wedding caterers are celebrated artisans, and no Surati wedding is complete without undhiyo, sev tameta, and at least three varieties of mithai.",
