    history: "Surat has a rich tradition of Sufi music and qawwali gatherings that reflects the city's deep history of Islamic culture, scholarship, and spiritual expression. Qawwali — the devotional music of the Sufi tradition — is performed at dargahs (shrines) across the city, particularly at the Dargah of Hazrat Makhdoom Yahya Maneeri and several smaller shrines in the old city. These performances, typically held on Thursday evenings and during significant Islamic occasions, involve passionate vocal performances accompanied by harmonium and tabla, with the music building in intensity over several hours to create a deeply trance-like spiritual atmosphere. Surat's Sufi musical tradition is distinct from the more Bollywood-influenced qawwali popular elsewhere, preserving classical Persian and Urdu compositions.",
